        "The preferred view across ALL FOUR Fiqh schools (Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'e, Hanbali) is that Tawarruq is permissible, though Qard al Hasan (interest-free lending) remains more preferable where available.",
        "AAOIFI's ruling: selling the commodity back to the original deferred-payment seller (directly or indirectly, even through an agent) is invalid; selling to a genuine third party is acceptable.",
