      commonConfusions: [
        "Students often think a Ju'alah worker who tries hard but fails still deserves some payment. The rule is strict: realization of the actual result is necessary for compensation - genuine effort alone, without success, earns nothing, unless the offeror separately revokes the contract mid-work (in which case a reasonable wage, not the full reward, is owed)."
      ],
